      "id": 1,
      "text": "In 2017, Concordia was officially named \"The Orphan Train Town\" to honor the historic orphan trains that once crossed the state.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.travelks.com/places-to-visit/cities/concordia/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The National Orphan Train Complex, located in the restored Union Pacific Depot, preserves the history of those trains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Concordia%2C_Kansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Brown Grand Theatre, a 1907 opera house now fully restored, sits on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.concordiakansaschamber.com/travel-tourism-historical"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Republican River Pegram Truss bridge, built in 1893 for Union Pacific, is a three‑span historic bridge on the National Register.",
